                  <handDesc>
                     <handNote xml:id="h1" script="Ethiopic">
                        <seg type="script">A nineteenth-century script (?)</seg>
                        <seg type="ink">Black, red (moderate red, moderate vermillion).</seg>
                        <desc>Mediocre, awkward, hard to read.</desc>
                        <seg type="rubrication">Divine names, name of the supplicants; several groups
                           of lines on the incipit page of <ref target="#ms_i1"/>, alternating with black lines; two
                           lines of the incipit of <ref target="#ms_i2"/>, <ref target="#ms_i3"/>, <ref target="#ms_i4"/>, <ref target="#ms_i5"/>, 
                           <ref target="#ms_i7"/>, <ref target="#ms_i8"/> and <ref target="#ms_i9"/>; first word of
                           <ref target="#ms_i6"/>; incipit of each section in <ref target="#ms_i1"/> and <ref target="#ms_i8"/>, incipit of each
                           miracle in <ref target="#ms_i2"/>, <ref target="#ms_i7"/> and <ref target="#ms_i9"/>, incipit of each strophe in Text <ref target="#ms_i3"/>. 
                           The word <foreign xml:lang="gez">ʾǝsaggǝd</foreign> (‘I worship’) in Text  <ref target="#ms_i4"/>; elements of punctuation
                           signs, text dividers and Ethiopic numerals.</seg>
                     </handNote>
                  </handDesc>
